            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Look for example use of blocking queue  - and test – but probably stop using waitable event. Maybe use condition variable, or review. DOCUMENT why safe to use wiatable event. It seems to just guarnateee waking up one thread, not all.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "       >>>>> MAYBE DONE",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "       >>> DOCUMENT MY “WAIT” on “AutoReset” event doesn’t guarantee ALL threads awakened and for manual reset, does guarantee all awkened, but not necessarily before any manual reset. So Auto-RESET DANGEROUS IF MULTIPLE THREADS WAITING – well – could be OK – but beware of this issue, and use condition_variable directly if you want to assure all threads awakend (so maybe I should just do that – but then need to implement q to assure all awakened???)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
